    ["src/games/updates/1316421563.txt"] = [[
0.1.26 | The whole interface now renders on RedzLib, the vendored library in the repo (src/dephubv2lib.lua). The old theme was retired and the shared shell was rewritten as a thin adapter over RedzLib, so every game keeps the same tabs, sections and controls it had before -- look and behaviour did not change, only what draws them. Two things are visible: the open/close key is still N (the shell binds it itself, because RedzLib has no key binding of its own), and group rows now stack their controls vertically instead of side by side (RedzLib has no horizontal container; the controls are all still there, just one under the other). Blox Fruits island teleport also stops disarming by hand: once the character actually reaches the island you picked, that toggle turns itself off. It only flips on real arrival at that flight's destination (25 studs of the island), never starts early and never fires again after you have landed.
0.1.25 | Blox Fruits gains Island Teleport, a new Travel tab. Turn the toggle on, pick an island from the dropdown, and the character flies there. The toggle is a real gate: selecting an island while it is off only remembers the choice, and switching islands while it is on flies again. The destination is the real instance in the map (workspace.Map.<Name>) rather than a hardcoded coordinate, so it does not break when the map changes and it uses exactly the names the user confirmed; if the island is not in the map it says so instead of flying into empty space. The list is the Sea 2 set the user provided: Snow Mountain, Indra Island, Ice Castle, Green Bit, Grave Island, Ghost Ship Interior, Ghost Ship, Forgotten Island, Fishmen, Dressrosa, Darkbeard Arena and Dapper Jack Arena. It has no motor of its own -- it uses the shared teleport by injection, like the fruit feature does. No sliders.
0.1.24 | Blox Fruits fruit detection fixed for the fruits the game spawns. The feature only ever looked at Tools, but a fruit the game spawns into the map is a Model named Fruit/fruit with no Handle -- the Handle (and the ProximityPrompt) only appears once a player touches it. So a spawned fruit never got ESP and the grab never flew, while a fruit dropped by another player (which IS a Tool) worked -- exactly what the user reported. Detection now accepts both shapes: a Tool with OriginalName/Handle, and a Model (or Part) whose name is Fruit-like. ESP also stops orphaning its highlight: the fruit part can change while the fruit exists, and the old code reused the entry and left the adorner pointing at a dead part, which was the glitch the user saw; it now re-targets the adorner when the part changes. The grabbed spawned fruit is reached by flying onto it -- touching it is what makes the game turn the Model into a collectible Tool, so the grab does not refuse just because there is no prompt yet.
0.1.23 | Blox Fruits raid is parked. The raid feature was not behaving the way the user needs and he is going to rebuild it from scratch, so the whole thing was taken out of the active list rather than left half-working: src/games/features/bloxfruits/raid.lua moved to features/bloxfruits/parked/raid.lua (nothing deleted), the RAID section and both toggles (Auto raid, Auto complete raid) are gone from the Farm tab, and the raid is out of the manifest so it no longer loads, instantiates or bundles. The blade hit and the fruit feature are untouched. The backend keeps the combat injection slot in the feature context, reserved for whoever attacks through the shared blade hit next.
0.1.22 | Auto complete raid no longer picks islands by distance -- it walks them by number. The user checked the map with Dex and confirmed the islands are workspace.Map.RaidMap.RaidIsland1, RaidIsland2, RaidIsland3..., so the number IS the order, and "nearest" was the wrong idea: it could fly to an island that is close but out of sequence. Now it starts on island 1, stays while that island still has a live mob, advances to the next number only once it is clear, and when there is no next island AND no mob left alive it calls the round over: it stops acting and just waits, letting the game close the round on its own. It never restarts anything. Mobs are looked for in Workspace.Enemies and Workspace.Characters and inside the current island. Starting the toggle resets the sequence to island 1.
0.1.21 | Blox Fruits raid gets a second, narrower toggle: Auto complete raid. Where Auto raid buys the chip, flies to the tube and starts the raid, Auto complete finishes a raid that is already running -- and does nothing else. It reads the islands under workspace.Map.RaidMap, flies to the one nearest the player right now, lets the blade hit kill the mobs, then recalculates and moves to the next nearest, so it advances one island at a time instead of jumping around. No owner filter: it picks purely by distance, as the user specified. It holds off re-issuing the flight while already close (under 40 studs) so the character does not vibrate in place fighting the tween. The toggle turns the blade hit on when it reaches an island and turns it off again when switched off -- but only if the complete turned it on; a blade hit the player enabled stays enabled.
0.1.20 | Blox Fruits gains its auto raid, built on the two motors the script already has instead of new ones. features/bloxfruits/raid.lua runs the whole cycle the old events.lua did: it makes sure a Microchip is in hand (asking the raid NPC to buy the one for the chosen element when it is not), flies to the raid tube with the shared teleport motor, equips the chip again on arrival and fires the tube button through fireproximityprompt, and once the server says the raid started (the Raids remote's StartTimer event) it starts clearing waves -- by driving the blade hit it was handed, never by firing its own attack, so there is one attack motor in the script, not two. Injection just grew a second piece: every feature now gets {teleport, combat, state}, where combat is the blade hit when it exists; without a teleport the raid refuses outright, and without the blade hit it still enters but reports that it has nothing to attack with. The raid picks its tube by sea (ReplicatedStorage.Util.Realm, the same source the old script used), with the Microchip element selectable from a dropdown. Also: the fruit tab moved under the Farm category -- a fruit picker and a raid runner are both Farm, not two categories for one game.
0.1.19 | Blox Fruits gets its fruit feature, built on the shared teleport motor. features/bloxfruits/fruit.lua covers Grab, ESP and Store: it finds ground fruits (a Tool in Workspace carrying OriginalName and a Handle), highlights them with a distance label, flies to the nearest with the teleport motor and fires its ProximityPrompt, and stores held fruits through the CommF_ remote while respecting a never-store list. The point is the integration the user asked for -- the fruit does NOT roll its own teleport, it receives the motor as a context at creation (options.teleport) and calls tp:GoToInstance(handle); without a motor the ESP and store still work and only the grab refuses. Everything else the old fruits.lua mixed in (gacha, dealer, awakening, chests) stays out. The backend now builds its panel from a per-feature PANELS table (category, tab, section, controls) instead of hardcoding one feature, and passes each feature a context with the teleport motor.
0.1.18 | Blox Fruits gains its teleport motor, and the blade hit loses its sliders. features/bloxfruits/teleport.lua is the open-source fly, ported to the own-module shape with no UI and no toggle: it is infrastructure, not a panel feature. State:Teleport() publishes it to every feature (and the console) already enabled, so a fruit-picker can call tp:GoToInstance(part) or tp:GoToIsland("Jungle") to move the character -- one tested teleport instead of each feature re-implementing its own. Go tweens the HumanoidRootPart with duration scaled by distance, zeroes the linear velocity and noclips during the flight (never Anchors: BF rejects every hit on an anchored root), and carries the full island/boss tables for all three seas. GoToInstance accepts a BasePart or Model, which is the contract a world-scanning feature hands it. The blade hit now exposes only a toggle: range defaults to 300 and the interval to 0.05s -- the strongest that still works -- set on the module (SetRange/SetInterval remain for the console) but with no sliders in the panel.
0.1.17 | Blox Fruits keeps only the blade hit. Every other feature the user took out was moved to features/bloxfruits/parked/ with git mv -- nothing deleted, just out of the active folder -- and parked means parked: not loaded, not instantiated, not in the manifest, not in the bundle (bundle.js now skips that subtree). The global DISABLED flag and its __DEPHUB_BF_DISABLED test override are gone: there is no switch that turns the whole game off, what loads is exactly what is listed in FEATURE_MODULES, and a parked feature is rejected as an unknown name like any other. The backend also lost its now-meaningless parked state from State and GetStatus.
0.1.16 | Blox Fruits is now the user's own script, feature by feature. The backend no longer loads the vendored open-source tree (oss/): it loads one self-contained file per feature from features/bloxfruits/, each doing its own game:GetService and publishing new()/Enable()/Disable() with no DepHub dependency, and it only downloads the tree, builds the panel and flips the toggle. The blade hit comes back first as features/bloxfruits/bladhits.lua: it fires the game's own RegisterAttack/RegisterHit at every enemy in range on a jittered loop, resolves the remotes through Modules.Net with a ReplicatedStorage.Net fallback, refuses cleanly when they are absent, and carries the server-validated hitId as the second remote's 4th argument. Range and interval are set on the module itself (SetRange/SetInterval) rather than through a parallel config on the backend. The oss/ files stay on disk but are no longer tracked or bundled.
0.1.15 | Blox Fruits is turned off -- by request, and nothing was deleted. One master switch (DISABLED = true in src/games/bloxfruits.lua) parks the whole backend: no module initialises, so no feature registers a control, and the frontend is never built, so no tab, section, category or sea category from Blox Fruits appears in the panel. Every file stays committed and downloadable, the loader still routes the two place ids and the backend still returns its State, so the Debug tab reports "BloxFruits.Enabled = no" and explains how to turn it back on. Set DISABLED = false to restore the whole tree exactly as it was.
0.1.14 | Back to Blox Fruits: two features from the old script return. Blade hits auto-swings the equipped weapon at every enemy in range by firing the game's own attack remotes (RegisterAttack + RegisterHit) on a jittered cadence, with sliders for range and interval (ms) and switches for the Enemies/Characters folders and nearby players; the hit carries the server-validated hitId, which it now follows on every capture instead of reusing a stale one. Flashstep (no cooldown) keeps the character's FlashstepCooldown attribute pinned at zero so the move is always ready, and rebinds on respawn. Both sit in the panel (Blade hits in PVP, Flashstep in Player) and clean up fully on unload.
0.1.13 | Fix: the Impulse slider was invisible in Volleyball's Jump feature. A slider shares a line (HStack) with the toggle, and the shell squeezed it to half width -- but the slider's internals are right-anchored with fixed offsets, so at half width its label collapsed and the -/+ buttons overflowed off the edge. Two fixes: the Jump toggle and slider now each take their own full-width line, and the shell's row layout refuses to squeeze a slider (it keeps full width instead of sharing the line).
0.1.12 | Volleyball 4.2 gains its first feature since the restart: Jump Anywhere. One toggle turns on both the jump bypass (patches the game's CharacterActions.Jump check so it stops vetoing jumps) and the extra impulse that speeds the jump up; one slider sets the impulse strength (0-150%, 0% keeps the original jump). With no executor debug.getupvalue/setupvalue the bypass cannot apply, so the toggle reports it and the backend keeps running. It sits in a Movement tab and is fully restored on unload.
0.1.11 | Volleyball 4.2 restart: every feature was removed from the backend to start over. Gone: ball prediction, auto position, forced jump, ceiling noclip, Auto Set Aim, the fixed set parts, the whole tab UI and the backend's own diagnostics. What stays is the game-action automation -- the actions.lua module and State:Act(name, ...) -- so set (front/back), spike, block, bump, dive, spawn ball and serve remain available to whatever features come next.
0.1.10 | The loader is quiet on the console now: a healthy load prints exactly one line, "DepHub v<version>", instead of the startup chatter (executor, place, host, progress). That detail is still recorded in full for the Debug tab. Real failures (a backend that threw, an unknown place, a reload that did not take) still surface through warn so a broken run is never silent.
0.1.09 | Two crashes fixed now that the current build actually loads. Auto Set Aim hooked PlayerAction.FireServer by assigning the field, but a Roblox Instance keeps its methods on a shared metatable, so the assignment raised "FireServer is not a valid member of RemoteEvent" the moment the toggle was flipped. It now intercepts the method through the executor's hookfunction (restoring with restorefunction) and only falls back to a field patch for plain-function doubles. Separately, the shared shell exposed AddHStack/AddVStack on the library instead of the section handle, so Blox Fruits failed to build with "attempt to call missing method 'AddHStack'". The wrapper now calls the section handle, and the test double was corrected to model a real Instance (methods are not assignable) so this class of mismatch cannot pass offline again.
0.1.08 | Loader: pick the source host that actually serves this build. The host probe accepted the first mirror whose version.txt would parse, so a mirror stuck on an old cache (jsDelivr kept answering) could win and load a tree missing every new feature -- the parts, Auto Set and the panel global simply were not there. raw.githubusercontent.com is now probed first and a host is accepted only when its version.txt is EXACTLY this loader's version; a stale mirror is skipped instead of silently chosen.
0.1.07 | Shared UI: a keyboard-independent way to open the panel. The shell's toggle key is discarded when the executor reports the keypress as gameProcessed (which some executors, including Madium, do), leaving the panel impossible to open from the keyboard. A new global __DEPHUB_TOGGLE() opens or closes the panel directly from the console, and doubles as a probe: if it works but the key does not, the executor is dropping the keypress.
0.1.06 | Loader: the second blocking wait is gone and startup is no longer silent. The loader gated startup on 'game.Loaded:Wait()', which never returns once the game has already loaded -- the same hang as the removed PlayerAdded wait, and the reason a run could reach the identity lines and then stop with no panel. It now polls game:IsLoaded() with a bounded active wait instead. The loader also logs progress around the UI and backend load and a final ready line, so a run is never a black box between 'Source:' and the window appearing.
0.1.05 | Loader fix: no more silent startup. The loader used to declare 'Players.LocalPlayer or Players.PlayerAdded:Wait()' and never use it -- when LocalPlayer was nil at run time that :Wait() blocked the whole thread, with no print, no error and no panel (the 'I ran it and nothing happens' symptom). The dead declaration is gone. The loader now also prints a liveness line before any early return, and a repeat run of an already-healthy session logs 'Already running vX (session healthy); skipping reload' instead of returning true in silence.
0.1.04 | Volleyball 4.2: Auto Set Aim. A new toggle in the Ball Predict tab's Set Assist section: while it is on, the exact instant a set fires ('Setting'/'Backsetting' through ReplicatedStorage.Remotes.PlayerAction) the character's body turns to face the nearest of the two fixed set positions. Only the body turns and only at that instant -- it does not stay facing there -- and the turn is yaw-only (the character never tilts up or down) and never moves the character. Implemented by wrapping the remote's FireServer while the toggle is on; spike/block/spawn/serve never trigger it, and disabling or unloading restores the original FireServer exactly. New Debug read (AutoSetAim).
0.1.03 | Volleyball 4.2: the game's action remotes are mapped and exposed. A new feature module (features/volleyball/actions.lua) drives the real game paths -- FireServer on ReplicatedStorage.Remotes.PlayerAction and LoadAnimation on the character's Animator -- for a front set ('Setting') or backset ('Backsetting'), spike ('Spiking'), block ('Blocking'), bump and dive (animation only), SpawnBall ('SpawnBall','Spawn') and serve ('SpawnBall','Serve' then 'Serving' after the game's 1.2s delay). The equipped animation index is read from PlayerData at runtime instead of a hardcoded id, and an absent remote/animator degrades to a reported failure instead of erroring. Exposed as State:Act(name, ...) for the automations, with new Debug probes/reads (PlayerAction, ActionAnimations, Actions). Cancels an in-flight serve on unload.
0.1.02 | Volleyball 4.2: auto SET. Two fixed set positions are created in the Workspace as soon as the backend loads -- 1x1x1 anchored, non-colliding parts at (-22, 15, 0) and (22, 15, 0), inside their own folder (DepHubAutoSet). There is no control for them: they cannot be switched off, they simply exist while the script runs, and unloading removes the folder with the parts.
0.1.01 | Shared UI (every game): sections now hug their content. A section's height is the measured content of its body, and since that measurement already includes the body's own padding the old size added an extra 24px of dead space under the last control -- the empty band that showed up at the bottom of a section. Removed. Also added real VStack/HStack grouping: related controls sit side by side on one line (a toggle next to the slider that drives it, the switches of one feature together) across Volleyball 4.2, Universal, Violence District, TSB, MM2, Noob Piece, AOT:R, Blood Strike, Steal An Egg, Restaurant Tycoon 3 and Blox Fruits, so tabs are shorter and less cluttered. New shell primitives AddHStack/AddVStack, exposed as Kit.Row/Kit.Stack, with tests.
0.1.00 | Shared UI (every game) + Debug: full English pass. Every player-visible string -- tab names, section titles, toggle/slider labels, paragraphs, notifications, status reads and the Debug console vocabulary ([FAIL], module/probe details, command replies) -- is now English (was Portuguese). Docs and code comments stay in Portuguese. Also the default open/close key is now N. The Debug tab, loader notes and backend diagnostics all read in English.
0.0.99 | Volleyball 4.2: reorganised by category -- ball prediction and auto-position (Visual), jump helpers (Movement) and ceiling collision (World).
0.0.94 | Shared UI (every game): fix the mouse getting stuck when the panel is closed. The game's cursor state (MouseIconEnabled + MouseBehavior) is now captured afresh every time the panel opens and restored by one shared path on Toggle close, Minimize and Destroy, so it can no longer hand back a stale value and leave the OS cursor hidden. The render loop also no longer touches the mouse while the panel is minimized/closed, so hovering the restore pill can't hide the cursor out from under the game. Adds a regression test for the open/close hand-back.
0.0.93 | Volleyball 4.2: merge the jump controls. Jump Boost and Jump Bypass were the same operation (set the jump power and keep the jump usable), so they are now one toggle 'Pulo forcado' with a single Jump Power slider; the second slider and the second toggle are gone, and Auto Jump stays as a sub-option. Adds AGENTS.md with the project rule: build the minimum that works, merge duplicate controls, do not create anything that does not need to exist.
0.0.92 | Volleyball 4.2: remove Look at Ball, Turn to Ball, the court gating and the hitbox (with its Part), keeping the ball prediction, Auto Position (Instantaneo + smoothness), Jump Boost/Bypass and Ceiling no-clip. The panel is reorganised into two balanced columns: Previsao + Auto Position on the left, Pulo + Colisao on the right.
0.0.91 | Volleyball 4.2: revert the move-mode change. Auto Position goes back to its simple smooth-or-instant behavior (the Instantaneo toggle plus the movement-softness slider); the Teleport/Instantaneo/Walk dropdown and the Walk-speed slider are gone. Everything else from 0.0.88 stays: yaw-only look and turn, court gating, hitbox, and Ceiling no-clip. The Part Visible fix from 0.0.89 is kept.
0.0.90 | Loader: resolve the source host per session. The loader no longer trusts raw.githubusercontent.com, whose branch edge cache can serve a whole revision behind and left the loader (and every module) stuck on the previous build; it now probes jsDelivr first, then github.com/raw, then raw, keeps the first host serving the current version, and publishes that base to every module. Also fixes the PositionHitbox Visible error from 0.0.89.
0.0.89 | Volleyball 4.2 fix: the position hitbox is a Part, which has no Visible property, so setting it errored the whole backend ('Visible is not a valid member of Part'). It now shows and hides through Transparency. The test harness rejects GUI-only members on non-GUI instances so this class of bug fails the suite instead of only in the game.
0.0.88 | Volleyball 4.2 assistance overhaul: Olhar pra bola and a new Virar o personagem now only rotate on the horizontal axis (never tilt up/down) and only act inside the green court areas; Auto Position gains a Teleport/Instantaneo/Walk move mode with a Walk speed slider, a court check, and an optional visible hitbox so it only chases landings it can actually reach. Ceiling parts are non-colliding for the player by default (restored when off).
0.0.87 | Volleyball 4.2 Jump Bypass: a toggle that re-applies JumpPower, JumpHeight and the jumping state every frame so a no-jump zone cannot block you, plus a configurable bypass power, an Auto Jump toggle that jumps for you, and a live Debug check of whether the humanoid can currently jump. Turning it off restores the game's original jump values and states.
0.0.86 | Volleyball 4.2 ball prediction: improved confidence (works with zero-config gravity) plus new assistance controls -- Auto Position walks the character to the predicted landing point (smooth by default, an Instantaneo toggle snaps it), Olhar pra bola keeps the camera on the ball, and Jump Boost overrides the humanoid jump power and restores the game's original value on toggle-off or unload. New distance gate for prediction, and the assistance features are covered by a new backend test suite.
0.0.85 | Blox Fruits: raid pacing, player ESP range, fly speed, persisted waypoints, legendary poll interval, extras summon wait, plus panel descriptions, feature search and automation status.
0.0.84 | Blox Fruits fruits: cap the fruit ESP distance, limit how far fruits are auto-collected, skip specific fruits on pickup, keep chosen fruits out of the auto-store, and set the chest cooldown.
0.0.83 | Blox Fruits config: delete, rename and reset a saved config, plus reset every control to its default or just one module at a time. The test harness now has an in-memory filesystem and JSON codec, so Save/Load is actually covered.
0.0.82 | Blox Fruits PVP: aimbot gains a max range and a body-part picker, the skill rotation follows a configurable order (it used to fire in random order every session), and Auto Bounty takes an ignore list.
0.0.81 | Blox Fruits farm: two real tuning sliders (Approach distance and Attack interval) that write straight through to the farm config. A slider with a fractional range now keeps its precision instead of rounding every value to a whole number, so an interval like 0.35s is actually reachable.
0.0.80 | Blox Fruits: the sidebar now shows only the sea you are in plus the shared pages. On Sea 2 that means GENERAL and SEA 2 -- the combined SEA 1/2 and SEA 2/3 categories are gone. Features shared by more than one sea (Travel on Sea 1/2, Events and Fruits on Sea 2/3) are re-filed under the current sea, so nothing disappears; the sea categories also got their own icons.
0.0.79 | Steal An Egg (place 107778070777162): teleport ported from Blox Fruits -- a CFrame tween fly that glides the HumanoidRootPart to the target at a set fly speed, zeroing linear velocity and stripping collision during the move (noclip) while never anchoring the character. Targets are saved in game as waypoints (persisted to disk when the executor exposes file IO, otherwise kept in memory), because the map coordinates are not known ahead of time. Controls live in a fixed Teleport tab.
0.0.78 | New backend for Steal An Egg (place 107778070777162): the walk-speed feature ported from the Blox Fruits player module, and only that -- a "Speed boost" toggle and a "Walk speed" slider (16-300, default 50) driven by a RenderStepped loop that re-applies the value every frame, so the game controller cannot overwrite it. Controls live in a fixed Speed tab.
0.0.77 | New backend for Blood Strike (place 114234929420007): a character ESP that reads fighters from workspace.Characters (Models named after their owner) with a fallback to the standard Players surface, plus a team check, range, and name/distance/health/chams options. Controls live in a fixed ESP tab.
0.0.76 | Every game now gets a fixed Dashboard tab built by the loader itself, so the same home screen shows no matter which backend runs: the player greeting card (avatar, name, clock) plus the game/server card, and live performance metrics (framerate, latency, players, session). It reuses the library's own dashboard builders, so there is no game-specific code.
0.0.75 | The shared UI theme was split into ten ordered modules under src/core/ui/theme/ (data, sub-tabs, constructor, theme-apply, notifications, window, extras, public-api, controls, lifecycle); the orchestrator loads them in the original section order and each adds its methods to the one Library table, so behaviour is unchanged while the 13k-line file is now maintainable in pieces.
0.0.74 | The real UI theme is now covered by an automated test: the suite loads the actual demon-theme.luau (not the stub the backend tests use), builds a window against a Roblox double, then creates a category, tab, section and controls and destroys it, so a theme regression fails the suite instead of only showing up in-game.
0.0.73 | The Debug tab and the print/warn log hooks are now opt-in and off by default, so the hub runs clean in every game; the collector and every backend probe keep running underneath. Set env.__DEPHUB_ENABLE_DEBUG = true before loading, call __DEPHUB_DEBUG() live, or use the debug on|off console command to bring the tab back without reloading.
0.0.72 | The universal backend now builds its own UI in the shared shell (Movement, Visuals, Combate, Social, Servidor, Status) and instruments the Debug tab with its own probes, features and commands, so an unmapped game gets working controls and live diagnostics instead of an empty window.
0.0.71 | The loader now self-heals a stale bootstrap: when the remote version is newer than the cached build the executor served, it re-fetches DepHub.lua with a cache-bust token and re-executes it once, guarded against looping, so a fixed bootstrap URL never runs an old loader again.
0.0.70 | An unrecognised game now loads the universal backend automatically instead of stopping on the empty unsupported state; set env.__DEPHUB_DISABLE_UNIVERSAL to true to opt out and get the plain unsupported window back.
0.0.69 | The FPS metric now resolves through three routes in order -- FrameRate:GetValue(), FrameRate.Value, then the engine physics frame rate -- so it no longer sits at 0 on executors where FrameStats.FrameRate is exposed as a value object rather than a plain number.
0.0.68 | Module fetches now carry a per-session cache-bust token, so an executor's HttpGet cache can never serve a stale older revision of diagnostics.lua or any backend after main is updated. Also fixes the remote sniffer raising on an absent method and the Debug metrics crash when Stats members are missing.
0.0.67 | Remote sniffer no longer reads absent methods as raw indexes: a RemoteFunction has no FireServer and a RemoteEvent has no InvokeServer, so each method read is pcall-guarded and the absent one is skipped instead of raising and failing the whole backend load.
0.0.66 | Debug console metrics no longer crash when the executor does not expose Stats.FrameStats/Network: every optional Stats and Workspace read now resolves through FindFirstChild, so FPS/ping/titans degrade to no-data instead of raising.
0.0.65 | Every game backend now reports its own structure into the Debug tab: named instances, live feature state, watches and console commands, so a game update that breaks a dependency shows up as [FALHA] at the point of failure.
0.0.64 | Live Debug console: streaming log, live FPS/ping/memory/uptime metrics, feature state auto-refresh, warn/print/error hooks, remote sniffer and terminal commands in every game.
0.0.63 | Shared Debug tab: module health, game-structure probes, live feature state and a copyable diagnostic report in every game.
0.1.0 | Add Volleyball 4.2 ball prediction backend and DepHub mode selector

