0.1.10 | The loader is quiet on the console now: a healthy load prints exactly one line, "DepHub v<version>", instead of the startup chatter (executor, place, host, progress). That detail is still recorded in full for the Debug tab. Real failures (a backend that threw, an unknown place, a reload that did not take) still surface through warn so a broken run is never silent.
0.1.09 | Fixed the backend failing to load with "attempt to call missing method 'AddHStack'": the shared shell exposed the row/stack builders on the library object instead of the section handle the theme actually returns, so any CreateRow failed here. Row and stack grouping now goes through the section handle like every other control.
